# ── Phase 2 Integrations ──

# 1. Cloudflare Web Analytics (Free)
# Sign up at https://cloudflare.com → Web Analytics → Add your site
# Then paste the token you get here:
PUBLIC_CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN=your_cloudflare_analytics_token_here

# 2. Keystatic CMS (Free, GitHub Mode)
# To use Keystatic in production with GitHub auth, you need:
# - Create a GitHub OAuth App: https://github.com/settings/developers
# - Set the callback URL to your site (e.g., https://yasirrazaa.github.io/api/keystatic/github/callback)
# - Then set these environment variables in your Netlify dashboard:
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_oauth_client_id
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_github_oauth_client_secret
# KEYSTATIC_SECRET=your_random_secret_key

# Note: For local development, Keystatic works with 'local' storage mode (no env vars needed).
# In production, you'll need to set up a GitHub OAuth App and add these env vars to Netlify.

# 3. Follow.it Newsletter (Free)
# Sign up at https://follow.it
# Replace the form action URL in src/components/NewsletterForm.astro
# with your Follow.it subscription form URL

# ── How to use ──
# 1. Copy this file to .env:
#    cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your actual tokens
# 3. In Netlify dashboard, add these as environment variables (without PUBLIC_ prefix for Keystatic)
